NUMISONA diagnostics:
- SNR-ENG-001: NUMISONA: track `price`: time follows field `week`, which has role x (RFC-0001 §5).
- SNR-ENG-002: NUMISONA: track `price`: the instrument is `mallet`, the harmonic mallet-like default (SDR-29).
- SNR-ENG-012: NUMISONA: track `price`: field `price` reverses direction 8 times (1.3 per second), more than the up to 3 reversals studied; trend reversals hurt estimates more than density does (SDR-21). Add a `smooth` transform or slow the pace if the trend matters.
- SNR-ENG-004: NUMISONA: track `price`: loudness is constant at -18 dB, so pitch alone carries the data (SDR-23).
- SNR-ENG-003: NUMISONA: track `price`: notes last 0.25 s, the default duration (RFC-0001 §6).
- SNR-ENG-007: NUMISONA: track `price`: the tap count also encodes the pitch field, from 1 to 8 taps (A11Y-13).
- SNR-ENG-050: NUMISONA: track `price`: 17 notes play their taps faster than about 10 per second, where taps may fuse and stop being countable (SDR-20, experimental). Lengthen the notes or slow the pace.
